{"labs": [{"stimuli": [{"id": 0, "template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome", "_data": []}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe7n6le02ob07re2aud01", "coverimg": "enpe7n6le02ob07re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"id": 0, "image": "enpe7n6le02ob07re2img01.jpg", "text": "<strong>Mike:</strong> Luke, what's a string in PHP?</br>\n<strong>Luke:</strong> Basically, it's a type of PHP data considered as a sequence of 256 characters. </br>\n<strong>Mike:</strong> We can study together so that we will know what to answer in the exam.</br>\n<strong>Luke:</strong> Well, I've decided not to study that anymore because I simply don't understand. </br>\n<strong>Mike:</strong> But, the test is tomorrow. I swear you still miss studying all the functions to manipulate strings.</br>\n<strong>Luke:</strong> I wonder how to study that. There are too many!</br>\n<strong>Mike:</strong> Well, let's review some of them, and call it a day.</br>\n<strong>Luke:</strong> It sounds good!</br>", "time": "100"}, {"id": 1, "image": "enpe7n6le02ob07re2img02.jpg", "text": "<strong>Mike:</strong> So, tell me where to put the functions and the strings in PHP.</br>\n<strong>Luke:</strong> The string, which is a sequence of characters, goes in parenthesis, while the function has to go before the parenthesis. For instance, soundex( ) would be a good sample of it. </br>\n<strong>Mike:</strong> Now, tell me, what functions can you remember?</br>\n<strong>Luke:</strong> To start, there is a function that calculates the length of a string; I mean, it tells you the number of characters of that string. Then, another function counts the words in a string. Next, there is another one which is good for searching for specific texts within a string. In fact, the function that I prefer the most is strrev() because it reverses a string. For example, if you write \u201cMop\u201d and use this function, it will reverse it into \u201cPom\u201d.</br>\n<strong>Mike:</strong> So interesting!</br>", "time": "36000"}, {"id": 2, "image": "enpe7n6le02ob07re2img03.jpg", "text": "<strong>Luke:</strong> Yes. To continue, other functions can manipulate strings, so it allows you to replace text or characters; another one splits them into arrays, changes the letters to lowercase. Finally, there is a function that can randomly shuffle all the characters in a string, while others compare two strings. </br>\n<strong>Mike:</strong> Wow, it's difficult not to get confused with all that information. Remember not to strain yourself so hard about this. The teacher would not expect you to know all the functions.</br>\n<strong>Luke:</strong> I hope you're right about this.</br>\n<strong>Mike:</strong> I'm sure!</br>", "time": "92500"}]}, "type": "slideshow"}], "template_override": 1, "_data": []}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I can say what a string in PHP is.  ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can list some commonly used functions to manipulate strings. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can talk about characteristics of some commonly used functions to manipulate strings.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "Do you consider it's important to know how to replace texts in PHP? Why? ", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "What ways do you know to search for specific texts in PHP? Explain.", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct"}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask yo