plications for an operating system for personal computers in a range of work contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level. Exchanges simple information on web applications, and applications for operating systems for personal computers.", "type": "secondary_1"}]}, {"content": "enpe7n6le02ob07re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "swear", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to promise something that could be true", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I swear you still miss studying all the functions to manipulate strings.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le02ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "call it a day ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to finish the work for today", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(idiom)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Well, let's review some of them, and call it a day.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le02ob07aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "length ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "duration or extension of something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There is a function that calculates the length of a string, I mean, it tells you the number of characters of that string.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le02ob07aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "reverse", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make something the other way around", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If you write \u201cMop\u201d and use this function, it will reverse it into \u201cPom\u201d.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le02ob07aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "lowercase", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the writing of letters that does not contain capitalization", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Another one splits them into arrays, changes the letters to lowercase.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le02ob07aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "shuffle ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to re-organize randomly something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Finally, there is a function that can randomly shuffle all the characters in a string, while others compare two strings.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le02ob07aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Look for more information about string functions in PHP ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Create a chart where you include the function and its use. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Prepare a presentation in which you explain what to do and what not to do with each function.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your work with the class. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I understand what a String in PHP is. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I identify functions to manipulate strings in PHP. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about functions and their usage for strings in PHP.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my work with the class. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Position of Not With to + Verb", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the particle <strong>Not</strong> when you want to talk about a negative situation or event.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you have an infinitive form, the particle <strong>Not</strong> usually goes just before the preposition <strong>to</strong>.</br></br>  Look at the following structure:</br></br> <div align=\"center\">Statement + <b>not</b> + verb in infinitive form (to + verb)</div>  Examples:   </br><i> Remember <strong>not to</strong> use the string variable without the correct codes.</br> It's important <strong>not to</strong> confuse string variables with PHP operators.  </i>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I've decided not to study that anymore because I simply don't understand. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It's difficult not to get confused with all that information.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Questions Within Sentences: How to / Where to / What to", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use questions within sentences when you need to ask about certain information of a place, a process, or the way to do something. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "To make these indirect questions in a negative or affirmative sentence, follow this structure:</br></br>  Sentence + <strong>how to / what to / where to</strong> + verb in infinitive form+ complement </br></br>  In this case, we included some WH question words, followed by the preposition <strong>to,</strong> such as <strong><u>how to</u></strong>, <strong><u>where to</u></strong>, and <strong><u>what to</u>.</strong> Remember that the use of the wh-words depends on what you want to know. </br></br>  Examples</br><i> I need to ask <strong>how to</strong> reverse a string. </br> Let me know <strong>where to</strong> to go.  </br> I don't know <strong>what to</strong> do about exam of arithmetical operators. </i>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "So, tell me where to put the functions and the strings in PHP. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I wonder how to study that. There are too many! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We can study together so that we will know what to answer in the exam.", "type": "example"}]}]}